-11-12\"}, {\"id\": \"P04-008\", \"reparto\": \"edilizia\", \"stato\": \"approvato\", \"importo\": 1527, \"responsabile\": \"Rita\", \"data\": \"2026-11-13\"}, {\"id\": \"P04-009\", \"reparto\": \"impianti\", \"stato\": \"sospeso\", \"importo\": 9033, \"responsabile\": \"Sara\", \"data\": \"2026-11-14\"}]\nMeasurement series: [23, 75, 5, 76, 38, 47, 33, 14, 28, 14]\n\nKeep the answer concise: at most about 120 words, or the requested code or data. Do not include internal reasoning.","title_original":"Outlier · scenario 05","prompt_translation":{"method":"English task templates and deterministic context translation","sha256":"56ed122dd195b6b236f2d3f0a00a58e479f3ec502e5721a82de55c3174211edb","used_for_inference":false},"answer_en":"```python\nimport numpy as np\n\ndata = [23, 75, 5, 76, 38, 47, 33, 14, 28, 14]\narr = np.array(data)\n\n# Calcolo statistiche robuste\nmedian = np.median(arr)\nq1 = np.percentile(arr, 25)\nq3 = np.percentile(arr, 75)\niqr = q3 - q1\n\n# Soglie (regola 1.5 * IQR)\nlower_bound = q1 - 1.5 * iqr\nupper_bound = q3 + 1.5 * iqr\n\n# Identificazione outlier\noutliers = [x for x in arr if x < lower_bound or x > upper_bound]\n\nprint(f\"Mediana: {median}\")\nprint(f\"Q1: {q1}, Q3: {q3}, IQR: {iqr}\")\nprint(f\"Soglia inferiore: {lower_bound}\")\nprint(f\"Soglia superiore: {upper_bound}\")\nprint(f\"Outlier individuati: {outliers}\")\n```<|im_end|>","answer_translation":{"method":"literal structured/code response","service":"Google Translate","translated_date":"2026-10-16","source_sha256":"0db60c4ad472a1439aa20eaf429da1b9540042d09d8f6dcbb57ab3ecb282ccaa","sha256":"0db60c4ad472a1439aa20eaf429da1b9540042d09d8f6dcbb57ab3ecb282ccaa","used_for_inference":false,"editorial_changes":[]},"answer_literal_glossary":[{"original":"Calcolo statistiche robuste","english":"Compute robust statistics"},{"original":"Soglie (regola 1.5 * IQR)","english":"Thresholds (1.5 * IQR rule)"},{"original":"Identificazione outlier","english":"Outlier identification"}]}